    <!-- Architecture -->
    <section id="architecture">
      <h2>5. Core Architecture Details</h2>
      
      <h3>SPA Client-Side Routing Fix</h3>
      <p>To prevent <code>403 Forbidden</code> errors when reloading browser tabs directly on frontend URL routes (<code class="inline-code">/login</code>, <code class="inline-code">/explorer</code>, <code class="inline-code">/admin</code>), we registered these routes in <code class="inline-code">SecurityConfig.java</code> permitAll rules. This allows Spring Web to pass them directly to the resource chain in <code class="inline-code">SpaWebFilter.java</code>, which loads the React entry bundle and lets client-side routing resolve the view.</p>

      <h3>Auto-Seeding Database</h3>
      <p>On startup, <code class="inline-code">DataSeeder.java</code> checks the JPA database. If empty, it encodes the admin password (<code class="inline-code">admin123</code>) to create the default user and writes 30 production distributed design pattern rows (e.g. Saga Pattern, Horizontal Scaling, CQRS) with details, complexity, and examples.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- UI Design -->
    <section id="ui-design">
      <h2>6. Visual Guidelines (Glassmorphism & Theme)</h2>
      <p>The visual framework maps HSL tokens in <code class="inline-code">index.css</code> to Tailwind CSS v4 variables inside a custom theme container:</p>
      <pre><code>@theme {
  --color-background: hsl(var(--background));
  --color-foreground: hsl(var(--foreground));
  --color-border: hsl(var(--border));
  --color-primary: hsl(var(--primary));
}</code></pre>
      <p>To style container elements with a glass-morphic sheen, apply the following classes:</p>
      <pre><code>.glass {
  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
  backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
  border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);
}</code></pre>
    </section>
